Finally, the rain stops.
I come outside from the museum.
Now, the sky is clear.
I walk towards Fort Kochi beach.
There is a nice breeze here.
I see those famous Chinese fishing nets.
Many people are walking along this walkway.
I stand near the nets.
I look out at that sea.
When I first came here, I had a little fear.
That was a completely new place to me.
I did not know anyone here.
But now, everything is different.
This is like my own hometown now.
I like this place very much.
I sit on a bench there.
A calm evening.
I happily watch that sunset.
